# 1. Stop doing post-hoc text review; LLM-as-judge compounds hallucination risk
def govern_campaign(creative_brief, audience_spend_tier):
    # 2. Invert generation: model may only assemble pre-cleared, signed claim-tokens
    approved_claim_tokens = legal_registry.pull_verified_claims(creative_brief.product)
    draft = model.synthesize_connective_tissue(creative_brief, approved_claim_tokens)
    # 3. Deterministic AST parse: extract semantic claims vs rhetorical filler
    extracted_claims, style_layer = semantic_parser.extract_propositions(draft)
    # 4. Binary check on claims; failure here drops to human MLR instantly
    if not claims_registry.substantiates_all(extracted_claims, approved_claim_tokens):
        return route_to_legal(draft, reason='unanchored_performance_claim')
    # 5. Watermarking metadata is stripped by ad networks; force burned-in disclosures
    rendered_asset = compositor.burn_visible_ai_disclosure(draft, creative_brief.target_region)
    # 6. Route ambiguous tone/brand-drift strictly by blast radius (budget * audience risk)
    if audience_spend_tier.expected_impressions > RISK_CEILING:
        return route_to_brand_lead(rendered_asset, diff_only=style_layer)
    return dispatch_to_ad_server(rendered_asset)

Hush, don’t build one judge to bless each line before it goes;
First tier the harm, and automate just what the evidence shows.

Bind every claim to cleared sources, rights, and audience too;
When wording wanders past its bounds, awaken human review.

Keep proofs beside each asset, for its metadata may not stay;
Log versions and approvals where no platform strips away.

Test it on the harms we missed, and count each false “all clear”;
Brand meaning, law, and truth stay hard—the answer isn’t here.
